CrmSenderHelp=Choose the address this message is sent from: the default sender of the CRM, your own address, or the mailbox of the lead e-mail collector. Your mail server must accept that address as a sender, otherwise the message may be refused or marked as spam. Replies arrive in that mailbox, and the CRM only sees them if it is the one the e-mail collector reads. Your choice is kept for your next e-mails.
CrmAiTimeout=AI time limit (seconds, 10 to 600)
CrmAiTimeoutHelp=How long the e-mail editor and the step text button wait for the AI service before they give up. Dolibarr stops an outgoing call after 30 seconds (MAIN_USE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT), which a long e-mail asked of a reasoning model can exceed: this setting raises that limit for the CRM calls only, never below the Dolibarr one. The web server must allow it too (time limits of PHP-FPM, nginx or Apache).
CrmAiNoHttpTimeout=no answer after %s seconds, the time limit of %s seconds ran out. Raise the setting "AI time limit" in CRM → Setup → Parameters, and check that the web server allows a request that long.
CrmAiNoHttpNetwork=no HTTP answer after %s seconds, well before the limit of %s seconds, so the connection failed rather than timed out (name not resolved, connection refused or reset, TLS error, proxy or firewall). The exact error is in the Dolibarr log, on the line "getURLContent response array" (the log level must be Info or lower).
