CrmReplyStageTip=The stage a deal moves to when the prospect replies. One per pipeline: ticking it here unticks the others.
CrmReplyMovesDeal=Move a deal to the reply stage when the prospect replies
CrmReplyMovesDealHelp=When the answer of a prospect is recorded on an open deal (read from the mailbox by the e-mail collector, or marked by hand on an enrolment of an outreach), the deal moves to the stage of its pipeline marked as the reply stage ("Replied to outreach" by default), if it is still before that stage. It is then up to the salesperson to qualify it. A deal that is already at that stage or beyond it, or closed, does not move.
CrmErrorStageReplyClosed=The reply stage must be an open stage: it cannot be won or lost.
CrmErrorEnrolmentNotFound=Enrolment not found.
CrmSequencesIntro=Automated outreach is for prospecting at scale: each enrolled prospect receives the same planned series of e-mails, calls and tasks, spaced by delays counted from the enrolment, without anyone having to remember them. It is not a conversation: with the default settings, as soon as the prospect replies, the outreach stops by itself and the deal moves to the reply stage of its pipeline, where the salesperson takes it over to qualify it. The reply is detected when the e-mail collector records it on the deal, or when someone presses "Mark replied". A prospect is enrolled from its opportunity. Nothing runs until automated outreach is enabled, and dry-run lets you review what would be sent before anything really goes out.
CrmOutreachHelp=The automated outreach this lead follows and where it stands. A lead follows one outreach at a time: when it follows none, pick one below to enrol it. The enrolment takes effect when you save: the first step falls due after its delay, counted from that moment, and the next steps count from the same moment. The outreach stops by itself when the prospect replies or when the deal is won or lost.
